[36m(RolloutManager pid=6643)[0m [2026-09-29 03:56:05.594 rollout_manager] sglang_rollout.py:494 - Finish rollout: ["<|im_start|>user\nTim rides his bike back and forth to work for each of his 5 workdays.  His work is 20 miles away.  He also goes for a weekend bike ride of 200 miles.    If he can bike at 25 mph how much time does he spend biking a week?\nPut the final numeric answer in \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nWe are told the following information:\n\n- Tim rides his bike **back and forth** to work **for 5 workdays**.\n- His job is **20 miles away**, and he goes to work **a weekend bike ride** of **200 miles**.\n- His biking speed is **25 mph**.\n\nWe are to find how much **time he spends biking in a week**.\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-step calculation:\n\n#### 1. **Workdays**:\n- He rides to work for **5 workdays**.\n- Each trip is **back and forth**, so that's **2 trips per workday**.\n- Each trip = **20 miles** (round trip).\n- So, for 1 workday: $ 2 \\times 20 = 40 $ miles.\n- For 5 workdays: $ 5 \\times 40 = 200 $ miles.\n- Total biking during workdays: **200 miles**.\n\n#### 2. **Weekend bike ride**:\n- 200 miles.\n\n#### 3. **Total biking distance**:\n$$\n200 \\text{ (work)} + 200 \\text{ (weekend)} = 400 \\text{ miles}\n$$\n\n#### 4. **Time spent biking**:\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} = \\frac{400}{25} = 16 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{16} \\text{ hours}\n$$<|im_end|>"], label: 16, reward: 1.0
